Lab-3

LAB MANUAL
Title
Mapping Agile Manifesto to Practices
Tool Used: Taiga
Lab Duration: 2 Hours
Lab Type: Hands-on, Tool-based
Mode: Individual / Pair Work

1. Aim of the Lab
The aim of this lab is to help students systematically map Agile Manifesto values and principles to real Agile practices and implement those practices using the Taiga Agile project management tool.

2. Learning Objectives
After completing this lab, students will be able to:
Explain Agile Manifesto values and principles
Translate Agile principles into concrete Agile practices
Use Taiga features such as backlog, user stories, sprints, comments, and wiki
Demonstrate Agile concepts such as adaptability, collaboration, and continuous improvement
Critically analyze the role of tools in supporting Agile values

3. Prerequisites
Students should have:
Basic understanding of Agile methodology
Familiarity with Scrum roles
Access to a Taiga account (cloud or institutional)

4. Project Context
Project Title: Agile-Manifesto-Practice-Mapping
Project Scenario: Online Course Registration System (OCRS)
Note:
This project is used only for planning, mapping, and learning purposes.
No coding or software development is required.

